+1. E(i,x) = C(i,x)--L(i,x), for every i,x.
+2. C(i,x)--C(i,y), for every fixed i and every x != y; thus each core group is a clique.
+3. For i<j, C(i,x)--C(j,y) exactly when (y-x) mod p belongs to the listed set F_ij.
