The paper’s Theorem 1 explicitly provides a constructive polynomial-time method, defeating Track A. The retained cyclic-marker attempt also fails Track B: both its strongest recovery and “compact” route require the same 1,008 residue inspections plus 17 modular operations—1,025 operations total, above the 300-operation cap. See the [paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1406.2440).

